{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"square of a sum identity square of a sum identity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md","fileName":"Square of a Sum Identity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Square of a Sum Identity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Factoring and Algebraic Identities]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"square of a sum identity square of a sum identity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md","fileName":"Square of a Sum Identity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Square of a Sum Identity","heading":"Square of a Sum Identity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The square of a sum identity is\n\n$$(a+b)^2=a^2+2ab+b^2.$$\n\nIt follows by distributing ((a+b)(a+b)). Geometrically, a square of side (a+b) divides into squares of areas (a^2) and (b^2) plus two rectangles of area (ab).\n\nThe middle term is essential: exponentiation does not distribute over addition. The identity can expand a squared binomial, recognize a perfect-square trinomial, or support mental arithmetic by choosing a nearby convenient value.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"square of a sum identity square of a sum identity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Square of a Sum Identity.md","fileName":"Square of a Sum Identity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Square of a Sum Identity","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}